#For local run
First install Docker toolbox if on Windows Home
Run: docker-machine start default
Check with: docker-machine ls

#To create image
docker build -t training_cloud:1.0 .

#To run locally
docker run -p 5555:80 training_cloud:1.0

#To publish 
docker login #Make sure you have an account

docker tag [your-image]:[version] [your-dockerhub-user]/[repo]:[version]
docker push [your-dockerhub-user]/[repo]:[version] #Takes quite a bit of time

#Deploy on azure
host for private docker repo: index.docker.io

Useful commands:
- docker-machine ls
- docker ps
- docker ps -a
- docker stop <container name>
- docker rm <container name>
- docker images
- docker rmi <image name>
- docker run -p 5555:80 <image name>
- docker system prune
- docker logs -f <image name> : show real time standard output
- docker run -d <image name> : run in background
- docker attach <id>

- docker history <image name>
